# Line endings are CONTENT for the frozen letter sheet.
#
# `letter_senses.lock.json` pins the sha256 of `letter_senses.csv`'s RAW BYTES,
# so a CRLF→LF translation is a content change: it trips the freeze without
# altering a single field. It has happened once already — a Python
# `read_text()` round-trip silently rewrote all 60 line endings and made the
# whole file show as modified. Marking the sheet binary keeps git from
# normalizing it on any platform, and keeps the diff readable by leaving the
# real edits as the only ones.
data/references/letter_senses.csv -text

# The lock itself is ordinary text; only the file it measures must not move.
data/references/letter_senses.lock.json text eol=lf
